![](/weird-guys.png "A picture of a woman holding some birds in her hand up for inspection. She is not impressed.")

This is a list of weird little guys in the free software movement and adjacent
spaces. Request additions, removals, or changes [via
email](mailto:drew@ddevault.org); patches welcome.

**Don't harass these people!** Don't engage with them at all.

---

# [Alex Gleason]($heading.id("gleason"))

> []($block.attrs('weird-guy'))
> ![](/gleason.png "Alex Gleason performing an interesting gesture")
>
> **Known for**: nostr stuff
>
> Alex is a prominent figure in the nostr community, and an antagonist on FOSS
> social media platforms generally. He developed the software used for Truth
> Social, Donald Trump's fediverse
> thing,[[source]](https://www.reuters.com/technology/head-engineering-trumps-truth-social-app-resigns-2023-07-17/)
> and was banned from the Mastodon instance he used back in 2023 for being
> openly transphobic.[[source]](https://web.archive.org/web/20230330163111/https://blog.alexgleason.me/gab-block/)[[source]](https://web.archive.org/web/20230331173749/https://blog.alexgleason.me/trans/)
> Alex is financially supported by [Jack Dorsey](#dorsey) via the
> "andOtherStuff" collective.[[source]](https://techcrunch.com/2025/07/16/jack-dorsey-pumps-10m-into-a-nonprofit-focused-on-open-source-social-media/)
>
> This photo of him on the right is prominently displayed on his personal
> website.

