# [Brendan Eich]($heading.id("eich"))

> []($block.attrs('weird-guy'))
> ![](/eich.jpg "Brendan Eich")
>
> **Known for**: Mozilla co-founder, Brave browser, creator of JavaScript
>
> Brendan got a lot of flack several years ago, resigning as Mozilla CEO, after
> he donated a few thousand dollars to support California's Proposition 8, an
> initiative that would have banned same-sex marriage in California.[[source]](https://web.archive.org/web/20200425070742/https://blogs.wsj.com/digits/2014/03/28/three-mozilla-board-members-resign-over-choice-of-new-ceo/)
>
> After Mozilla, he moved on to co-found and lead as CEO the Brave Browser,
> which he used to push his own cryptocurrency micro-payments
> system.[[source]](https://web.archive.org/web/20200725110058/https://techcrunch.com/2017/06/01/brave-ico-35-million-30-seconds-brendan-eich/)
> He used Brave to support the hate website Kiwi Farms, which has been alleged
> to have instigated several suicides as a result of their harassment, working
> with their site admins to pose Brave as a safe and secure means for their
> members to access the site and conduct their harassment.[[source]](https://samambreen.wordpress.com/2019/08/16/an-open-letter-to-brendan-eich/)
> Kiwi Farms also took advantage of Brave's crypto scheme for funding, which was
> brought to Eich's attention and never corrected.[[source]](https://www.change.org/p/brendan-eich-brave-software-stop-providing-a-revenue-stream-for-white-supremacist-paedophiles)

