# [Daniel J. Bernstein]($heading.id("djb"))

> []($block.attrs('weird-guy'))
> ![](/bernstein.jpg "Daniel J. Bernstein")
>
> **Known for**: Popular cryptographic algorithms, e.g. Salsa20, ed25519; qmail,
> djbdns
>
> **Alias**: djb
>
> Daniel is an well-known and influential cryptographer and former visiting
> professor at TU/Eindhoven,[[source]](https://www.researchgate.net/scientific-contributions/Daniel-J-Bernstein-69944562)
> where he has worked with his wife, Tanja Lange, the chair of the coding theory
> and cryptology group there.[[source]](https://cc.win.tue.nl/staff.html)
>
> Daniel and Tanja are associates of [Jacob Appelbaum](#appelbaum)
> and served as his PhD advisors.[[source]](https://research.tue.nl/en/persons/jacob-r-appelbaum/supervised-student-theses/)[[source]](https://www.hyperelliptic.org/tanja/students.html)
> One of the students under Bernstein and Lange at TU/e, Henry de Valence,
> resigned from their PhD program in 2016 citing patterns of harassment, abuse,
> and bullying at the hands of Jacob, Daniel, and Tanja.[[source]](https://medium.com/@hdevalence/when-hell-kept-on-payroll-somewhere-is-where-you-are-f419d3022d0)

