> frequently writes on his website in defense of rapists, sexual harassment,
> sexual exploitation of minors, distribution of child sexual abuse material,
> and even bestiality and necrophilia. Stallman's behavior is
> extensively covered in The Stallman Report.[[source]](https://stallman-report.org/)

---

# [Tobias Lütke]($heading.id("lutke"))

> []($block.attrs('weird-guy'))
> ![](/lutke.jpg "Tobias Lütke")
>
> **Known for**: Shopify (co-founder & CEO), Ruby on Rails (core team)
>
> Tobias is a billionaire and personal friend of [David Heinemeier
> Hansson](#dhh), and raced as part of his team for Era
> Motorsport.[[source]](https://www.eramotorsport.com/post/era-motorsport-announces-chatin-dalziel-hansson-and-l%C3%BCtke-for-rolex-24-lineup)
> He has a 40% controlling interest in Shopify.[[source]](https://www.yorku.ca/laps/newsroom/2026/07/31/shopify-ceo-tobi-lutke-calls-pensioners-dependents-who-shouldnt-get-to-vote-then-agreed-those-who-pay-500000-in-tax-should-get-5-votes/)
>
> Tobias defended Shopify's choice to platform (and therefore directly
> financially support) far-right tabloid Breitbart in 2017,[[source]](https://corporateknights.com/issues/2025-04-spring-issue/how-shopify-went-from-canadas-tech-darling-to-anti-dei/)
> citing freedom of speech and resisting the idea of implementing a "moral code"
> for Shopify clients. He also endorsed a proposal to strip retirees of voting
> rights and make votes proportional to wealth.[[source]](https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/shopify-ceo-endorses-idea-to-give-more-votes-to-wealthy-canadians-9.7286688)

# [Vincent Canfield]($heading.id("cockli"))

> []($block.attrs('weird-guy'))
> ![](/cockli-guy.jpg "Vincent Canfield")
>
> **Known for**: cock.li
>
> Vincent is the owner of the "cock.li" email provider, which provides
> intentionally "edgy" email addresses to its users and targets bigots and
> extremists who would be marginalized elsewhere with its free speech absolutist
> principles. The domain names available include options such as "@n\*gge.rs"
> and "@rape.lol", as well as a number of more covert domain names such as
> "@airmail.cc" which are more likely to fly under the radar.

